  "question": {
    "text": "The half-life period of a radio-active element $\\mathrm{X}$ is same as the mean life time of another radioactive element $\\mathrm{Y}$. Initially they have the same number of atoms. Then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "lVLVx",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{X}$ will decay faster than $\\mathrm{Y}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "40TyA",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{Y}$ will decay faster than $\\mathrm{X}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "7QF68",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{X}$ and $\\mathrm{Y}$ have same decay rate initially\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HhwnK",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{X}$ and $\\mathrm{Y}$ decay at same rate always.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{t}_{1 / 2}=\\frac{\\ln 2}{\\lambda_{\\mathrm{x}}}$\n$\\tau_{\\text {mean }}=\\frac{1}{\\lambda_{\\mathrm{y}}} ; \\frac{\\mathrm{dN}}{\\mathrm{dt}}=-\\lambda \\mathrm{N}$\n$\\frac{\\ln 2}{\\lambda_{\\mathrm{x}}}=\\frac{1}{\\lambda_{\\mathrm{y}}} \\Rightarrow \\lambda_{\\mathrm{x}}=\\lambda_{\\mathrm{y}}(0.6932) \\Rightarrow \\lambda_{\\mathrm{y}}>\\lambda_{\\mathrm{x}}$",
